    "always": true,
    "onTextChange": true,
    "rect": { "sizeDelta": [1000, 160] },
    "tmp": { "autoSize": true, "minSize": 40, "maxSize": 100, "wordWrap": false, "overflow": "Overflow", "alignment": "Center" }
  },
  {
    "id": "story-text-top-left",
    "comment": "Story dialog text (/StoryCore/SayDialogs/{Character,Narrative,Think}SayDialog/Panel/Background/StoryText, 1050x200 legacy Text, anchor/pivot (0,0.5) at ap (400,-20), prefab alignment UpperLeft, best fit 20-28). The box is lifted 26.9px (ap.y 6.9), so its top sits 19px below the frame top instead of 46px and three lines of English fit, and the text starts at the top-left corner like a book page. The original English patch's LOM_UI_Plugin_KR made the same lift on every SetActive but also set MiddleLeft, which floated one- and two-line English in the middle of the box; if it is installed, our OnEnable pass runs after its prefix. 'always' re-applies on every activation and onTextChange after each DoSay. The centred narration dialog (CenterNarrativeSayDialog, MiddleCenter by design) is not matched.",
